xnu 0129: bit-bang SPI on the touch pads

The GENI route is closed for this SE: the FIFO interface is disabled by the
firmware (GENI_IF_DISABLE_RO = 1) and the SE DMA path wedges the interconnect
(the boot stops right after the DMA buffer is announced), while GPI/GSI is a
driver of its own. For the first touch driver, clock the part from the TLMM
instead: GPIO16 clk, 17 mosi, 18 miso, 19 cs as GPIOs, mode 0, MSB first,
about 1 MHz from the 19.2 MHz timebase, CS driven by hand. The probe reads
the product id at 0x8140 in the two common framings.

Slow, but it does not depend on the QUP firmware and cannot wedge a bus.

